  "summary": "Bharathi Women's College in Broadway, North Chennai, was founded in 1964 as the Government Arts College for Women and renamed in 1981–82 for the centenary of the poet Subramania Bharathi. A Government college affiliated to the University of Madras, it became autonomous in 1998 and is re-accredited 'A' by NAAC; it has more than 4,000 students. It runs 13 UG programmes across two shifts, in English and Tamil medium; Edugate lists the programmes it has verified so far.",
